.\" XNote encrypted backup helper.
.TH XNOTE-CLOUD-BACKUP 1 "July 23, 2026"
.SH NAME
xnote-cloud-backup \- encrypted local and off-box recovery for XNote
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xnote-cloud-backup
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
XNote stores live notes as plaintext under
.IR ~/.config/xnote .
This helper creates authenticated encrypted snapshots under
.IR ~/.local/share/xnote-backup
and can append complete recovery kits to a filesystem or rclone remote.
Remote note contents are encrypted, but the provider can observe the device
name, snapshot timestamps, file sizes, count, and backup cadence.
.PP
Run
.B init
interactively once.  Preserve the printed recovery code separately from the
passphrase.  Without the passphrase or recovery code, encrypted snapshots
cannot be recovered.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Create the wrapped master key and print the one-time recovery code.
.TP
.B backup
Create a local snapshot and, when configured, upload an append-only recovery
kit.  An uninitialised helper or configured remote failure exits nonzero.
.TP
.B status
Show local snapshot count and the last remote attempt, success, or error.
.TP
.B list
List local snapshots.
.TP
.B remote-list
List complete remote recovery kits.  A manifest is the completion marker.
.TP
.BI "import " "ID|latest" " [--force]"
Download and validate a remote kit, then install its keyfile, head, and
snapshot into local recovery state.  Without
.BR --force ,
existing recovery state is refused.  With
.BR --force ,
the previous state is preserved under a
.I pre-import-*
directory.
The helper clears any cached master key and blocks new backups until the
imported keyfile is explicitly unlocked.
.TP
.B unlock
Prompt for the passphrase and cache the unwrapped master key.
.TP
.B unlock --recovery
Prompt for the one-time recovery code instead.
.TP
.BI "restore " "ID|latest" " [--force]"
Restore a local snapshot.  Close XNote first; use
.B --force
only when the caller has independently ensured that no live writer can race.
.TP
.B rotate-passphrase
Rewrap the unchanged master key under a new passphrase.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is read from
.IR ~/.config/xnote/cloud-backup.conf .
Recognised keys are:
.TP
.B KEEP_SNAPSHOTS
Number of local snapshots to retain (default 60).
.TP
.B CLOUD_REMOTE
An explicit filesystem path such as
.I /mnt/backup/xnote
or an rclone target such as
.IR dropbox:xnote-backup .
A bare word is rejected to prevent a misspelled remote from becoming a false
local success.
.TP
.B CLOUD_DEVICE
Stable remote device directory (default: current hostname).  Set this to the
original device name when recovering on a differently named replacement host.
.TP
.B CLOUD_TIMEOUT
Maximum seconds for each external transfer command (default 120).
.SH REMOTE LAYOUT
Each successful push appends:
.PP
.I <remote>/<device>/kits/<snapshot-id>/
.br
.I "  manifest.json"
.br
.I "  keyfile.json"
.br
.I "  head.json"
.br
.I "  snapshots/<snapshot-id>.xsnap"
.PP
The helper never automatically deletes remote history.  Provider-side
retention, if desired, must be configured independently and should preserve
multiple complete kits.
.PP
Only the manifest, keyfile, head, and manifest-named snapshot are downloaded.
Unexpected provider objects are ignored, and each expected object has a
hard size limit before it is accepted.
.SH DISASTER RECOVERY
On a replacement installation, install and configure rclone (if used), set
.B CLOUD_REMOTE
and
.B CLOUD_DEVICE
to the original device directory, then run:
.PP
.nf
xnote-cloud-backup remote-list
xnote-cloud-backup import latest
xnote-cloud-backup unlock
xnote-cloud-backup restore latest
.fi
.PP
Use
.B unlock --recovery
instead of
.B unlock
when recovering with the one-time recovery code.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/xnote/cloud-backup.conf
Configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/xnote-backup/
Keyfile, head state, local snapshots, lock, and remote status.
